          "id": "india-parliament-reconvene-2026-11-26",
          "headline": "Parliament to sit again: Lok Sabha on 30 November, Rajya Sabha on 2 December",
          "summary": "Parliamentary Affairs Minister Kiren Rijiju said the government has asked Speaker Om Birla and Rajya Sabha Chairman C.P. Radhakrishnan to reconvene both Houses for essential government business. The sittings may end on 3 December. The Monsoon Session was adjourned on 13 August but never formally closed, so these short sittings continue it; the agenda has not been announced.",
          "why_it_matters": "A short sitting before the year ends lets the government push through pending bills; which ones is not yet known.",
