          "id": "currency-rupee-slips-92-40-2026-11-26",
          "headline": "Update: Rupee closes 24 paise weaker at 92.44 per dollar",
          "summary": "New since midday: the rupee settled at 92.44 per dollar (provisional), down from Wednesday's 92.20, its best close of the financial year. It moved between 92.31 and 92.66. Crude near $95 and the proposed US tariff of up to 25% on Indian goods weighed, while foreign buying of Indian shares limited the fall. The RBI's reference rate at 1 PM was 92.48.",
          "why_it_matters": "The rupee's sharp recovery from its 96.88 record low in October has paused as oil and tariff risks return.",
